{"n": 436, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "436.webp", "text": "25-9\n\n2511111 REPLACING SHIFT ROD\nJOINT\n~Sheet Metal Shift Console—\n\nAccess to the shilt rod joint differs in\naccordance with the different transmis-\nsion and propeller shalt versions.\nRemove exhaust assy. - 18 00 020.\nRemove heat shield with reinforcement\ncarrier.\n\nVersion with 4 Speed Transmission:\nUnscrew console mounting bolts,\n\nimportant!\nSelf-locking bolis = will be difficult to\nunscrew.\n\nInstallation:\n\nUse new bolts coated with a micro-\nencapsulating cement.\n\nTightening torque’.\n\nVersion with 5 Speed Transmission;\nUnscrew propeller shaft on transmis-\nsion, see 26 11 000.\n\nVersion with 5 Speed Transmission and\nVibration Damper;\n\nUnscrew propeller shaft on transmis-\nsion, see 26 11 000,\n\nUnscrew output flange with vibration\ndamper on transmission, see 23 12 053.\n\n* See Specifications\n\n—\n\nr\n\nEngage reverse gear\nLift out ciretip (1)\nTake off washer (2)\nPull oul shift rod (3)\n\nPush back locking sleeve\n\nMove shift shaft to 3ra or Sih gear\nposition,\n\nDrive out pin.\n\nRemove shift rod with joint\n\nNote\n\ni shift rod joint has an offset bearing\nsleeve, Install the bearing sleeve offset\nto the right as seen looking forward.\nInstall offset to the left In cars with a\nvibration damper and bent shift rod.\n\ninstalation\nLubricate bearing surfaces with Klaber\nPolyup GLY 801\"*,\n\n“ Source of Supply: HWB", "words": [["25-9", 0.4651, 0.0298, 0.5187, 0.0536], ["2511111", 0.2786, 0.0681, 0.3281, 0.08], ["REPLACING", 0.3372, 0.0681, 0.4019, 0.08], ["SHIFT", 0.407, 0.0681, 0.4388, 0.08], ["ROD", 0.4439, 0.0681, 0.4671, 0.0787], ["JOINT", 0.3372, 0.084, 0.3696, 0.0959], ["~Sheet", 0.3372, 0.1019, 0.3736, 0.1138], ["Metal", 0.3777, 0.1019, 0.405, 0.1138], ["Shift", 0.409, 0.1019, 0.4338, 0.1138], ["Console—", 0.4378, 0.1019, 0.4884, 0.1138], ["Access", 0.2796, 0.1362, 0.318, 0.1481], ["to", 0.322, 0.1362, 0.3322, 0.1468], ["the", 0.3362, 0.1362, 0.3524, 0.14